Project Mu: never show Chromium's first-run welcome screen

The welcome ("The browser that gets more done") leads into browser sign-in and
sync, which Mu turns off. Upstream skips it when sign-in is disabled, but on a
new profile that check could run before initial_preferences were applied, so
the screen appeared on some first launches. Mu never opens it; the rest of
first-run processing, including initial_preferences, is unchanged.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/first_run_service.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/first_run_service.cc
index 7ba1ffb..1b951bf 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/startup/first_run_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/startup/first_run_service.cc
@@ -298,6 +298,12 @@ FirstRunServiceFactory::BuildServiceInstanceForBrowserContext(
 // Helpers ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 
 bool ShouldOpenFirstRun(Profile* profile) {
-  return IsFirstRunEligibleProcess() && IsFirstRunEligibleProfile(profile) &&
-         !IsFirstRunMarkedFinishedInPrefs();
+  // Project Mu: never show Chromium's first-run welcome ("The browser that
+  // gets more done"). It is a sign-in and sync funnel, and Mu has sign-in off.
+  // Upstream normally skips it when sign-in is disabled, but that check runs
+  // before a new profile's initial_preferences are applied, so it sometimes
+  // showed anyway. First-run processing itself (initial_preferences) still runs.
+  return false && IsFirstRunEligibleProcess() &&
+         IsFirstRunEligibleProfile(profile) &&
+         !IsFirstRunMarkedFinishedInPrefs();
 }
